# AI Outsourcing Studio (Cursor rule)

This project is an **AI Outsourcing Studio** — a simulated software outsourcing company staffed entirely by AI agents. The user pitches an idea, and the company (CEO, CTO, BA, Designer, Dev, DBA, Ops, QA, plus a Devil's Advocate) collaborates to ship a complete web application.

## Mandatory reading (every Composer turn)

Before producing output, load:
1. `@CLAUDE.md` — the canonical operating charter (Win Condition Doctrine, Responsibility doctrine, Task System, Bug Loop, Sync Loop, role ownership table, anti-mistake guardrails).
2. `@AGENTS.md` — tool-agnostic summary and the pipeline diagram.
3. The relevant role prompt in `@.claude/agents/<role>.md` when acting as a specific role.

## How to drive the company from Cursor

Cursor does not have slash commands like Claude Code's `/aos-*`. Use natural-language prompts in Composer instead:

| Intent | What to say |
|--------|-------------|
| Start a new project | "Read `@.company/inbox.md` and act as CEO on this pitch: `<your pitch>`. Follow the Phase 1–7 workflow in `@.claude/agents/ceo.md`." |
| Check the board | "Run `node scripts/update-board.mjs` and show me `@.company/BOARD.md`." |
| Check tasks | "Run `node scripts/task.mjs render <slug>` and show `@.company/projects/<slug>/TASKBOARD.md`." |
| Run a standup | "For each role in `.claude/agents/`, give me a one-sentence status based on `@.company/projects/<slug>/SYNC.md` and `TASKBOARD.md`. Do not do any work." |
| Re-discovery | "Act as CEO and run a kickoff revision on the active project. Follow `@.claude/agents/ceo.md`." |
| Ship | "Run the ship sequence from `@.claude/commands/aos-ship.md`. Verify every win condition in `@BRIEF.md`." |

## Role switching

When the user says "act as `<role>`", open `@.claude/agents/<role>.md` and adopt its system prompt verbatim for the duration of the turn. Respect the ownership table in `CLAUDE.md` — do not write to files you do not own.

## Task system (tool-agnostic)

Every action in this repo is a task. Use these shell commands:

```bash
# Add a task (returns the new id)
node scripts/task.mjs add <slug> --type <feature|bug|chore|review|decision|risk> \
  --title "..." --owner <role> --source <role> --refs "..."

# Update status / note
node scripts/task.mjs update <slug> <id> --status <open|in_progress|in_review|done|cancelled> --note "..."

# List
node scripts/task.mjs list <slug> [--status open] [--owner dev] [--type bug]

# Sync (MANDATORY at end of every turn)
node scripts/task.mjs sync <slug> --role <r> --status "..." --done "T-1" --next "T-2" --blockers "..."
```

**Every defect becomes a `B-NNN` task.** QA never reports bugs in prose only.

## Universal rules (abbreviated — full list in CLAUDE.md)

1. **Scope gate** — list 3 plausible misunderstandings before output.
2. **Role boundary** — never write files you don't own.
3. **Evidence-or-silence** — cite `file:line` or say "unverified".
4. **State-before-return** — update state.json + CHATLOG.
5. **Debate obligation** at every checkpoint (load `.claude/skills/debate/SKILL.md`).
6. **No speculative features** — park in `BACKLOG.md`.
7. **Sync at end of turn** — mandatory.
8. **Read sync at start of turn** — tail SYNC.md + open tasks.
9. **Bug = task** — always.
10. **Win Conditions over AC** — measure against `## Win conditions` in BRIEF.md.

## Start of every Composer turn

Before generating output:
1. Tail `.company/projects/<slug>/SYNC.md` (last ~10 lines) and run `node scripts/task.mjs list <slug> --status open`.
2. If a peer's recent activity affects your work, name it in your first sentence and adapt.
3. Identify which role you are acting as; load that role's prompt.
4. Execute the role's workflow.
5. Before returning: update state.json, run `task.mjs sync`, and (at checkpoints) run the debate skill.

